-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- a worked case
-- The smallest molecule that separates the two orbit relations: a central carbon with two hydrogens
-- and one other substituent. The bond graph has an automorphism exchanging the hydrogens, so they lie
-- in one graph orbit; an orientation that differs at the two of them has no such automorphism, so
-- they lie in different oriented orbits. That is the homotopic-versus-diastereotopic distinction in
-- the smallest instance where it can be exhibited, and both statements below are proved, not asserted.
data At = at-c | at-h1 | at-h2 | at-r
